  "body": "## What is needed\n\nPR #4475 (#3195) adds hole patterns from numbers through MCP (`add_hole_pattern`). The issue also asks for a form in the app. The form is not in that PR.\n\n## Design\n\n- Add a form that the Stock context and the Sketch context open. The form makes a Drill, Bore or Thread operation from a pattern:\n  - a point list;\n  - a line;\n  - a grid;\n  - a full or partial bolt-hole circle.\n- The form calls the same code as the MCP tool:\n  - `camcraft_geometry::hole_pattern::HolePattern::points()` for the hole centres;\n  - one undo group of `CreateOperation` commands, with the optional spot drill first.\n- Move the shared part of `crates/app/src/mcp/hole_pattern_tools.rs` (hole list, stock heights, the spot and main build) to an app-layer function. Then the UI and MCP use one door.\n- Let a Sketch of circles give the points: the circle centres and the circle diameter.\n- Show a preview of the hole centres before the user confirms.\n\nClean-room rule: use plain machining terms only. Do not copy vendor wording, labels or screen layouts.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe form makes each pattern on a stock-only setup in one undo step. A UI test asserts the labels, the roles and the command. The `crates/ui` test count does not go down.\n\nRefs #3195\n",
